{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/65794-demons-doing-non-demon-stuff","id":65794,"title":"Demons doing non-Demon stuff","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-05T10:19:32-08:00","id":65794,"title":"Demons doing non-Demon stuff","content":"So how often would everyone consider it appropriate for a group of demons to do things unrelated to the God-Machine. For example one of the group's Cover's sisters gets tangled up with some vampires and the demons decides to save her, bringing conflict with the vamps coterie. Or, while checking out a possible Infrastructure the group runs into, say, a mage investigating the same place. The group then decides to check out these mages to see how G-M influenced they are. Maybe a group of Demons is enhancing their Cover's presence in the Mafia or whatever, and end up butting heads with some Geist-having people (Geister?). Hell, they could even do something totally mundane like opening a fast-food chain or running for political office or something. I dunno, these are just ideas off the top of my head. Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T11:20:59-08:00","id":65825,"title":"","content":"One. Opening a fast food chain would relate to establishing a Cover; which, in itself, is very Demon-y. I'd totally be for it<br /> <br /> Two, dealing with other supernaturals happens on occasion - that is all setting dependent , depending on the table. Some games have massive crossover, which is superceeds almost all normal stuff for the game line. Other games have none.<br /> <br /> <br /> Three, there is no such thing as &quot;appropriate.&quot; Or, rather, the only appropriate depends on what kind of games does your local table enjoy playing. I personally don't care for a lot of crossover in my games, while others like more. Do your characters want to spend time establishing mortal, every day things, or they want to focus on the war against God?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T11:30:32-08:00","id":65833,"title":"","content":"I guess what I'm asking is this: the players could want to use their characters abilities to do something like found a criminal empire or fight the supernatural. Do people think this is setting appropriate or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T11:37:36-08:00","id":65838,"title":"","content":"Considering I consider the default of any game is actually &quot;Just getting by&quot;, I absolutely think that's appropriate.(I tend to like an almost slice-of-life take to my games, so if I can do that, your demons can confront Vampires or usurp McDonalds.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T11:50:05-08:00","id":65844,"title":"","content":"Sure, why not? Every demon finds Hell in their own way, and establishing themselves in the mundane world is a perfectly reasonable way to do so. For Tempters, this is basically just what you <i>do.</i> It should require some buy-in from the players, though; if one wants to focus on the struggle against the God-Machine and smashing its infrastructure, they may be frustrated if all their time is spent fighting vampires for control of the mob (unless control of the mob has a pointed goal--foot soldiers to send against the God-Machine, for example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1812-deflare","name":"Deflare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}